TUI diagnostic messages are cut off at narrow widths with no way to read the full text

Reported 2026-08-29 by Max from TUI use on a narrow terminal.

## Symptom
Error/warning messages in the TUI are truncated when the terminal is not wide
enough, and there is no way to see the rest of the text — no wrapping, no
horizontal scroll, no popup/expand. The diagnostic becomes unreadable exactly
when it matters (long "no matching signatures ..." messages are the worst).

Two separate cut points:

1. **List rows** — `ellipsize()` clips the message to the row budget and adds
   `…`. Compact: `msg_budget = content_w - (3 + loc + 2)`, so a long
   `path:line:col` steals the whole message. Relaxed: message gets its own row
   with `content_w - 3`, better but still one line.
2. **Detail box** — `pretty_detail_lines` pushes the message as a single
   `Line` and the pane renders with `Paragraph::new(lines)` and **no**
   `.wrap()` (src/tui/ui.rs:327-328 — deliberate, so the source line and the
   caret row stay column-aligned). Ratatui therefore hard-clips the message at
   the pane edge with no `…` at all, so the user cannot even tell text is
   missing.

## Cause
src/tui/ui.rs:
- `list_item_for` (~:476) — `ellipsize(&d.message, msg_budget)` for both
  densities; single-line by construction.
- `pretty_detail_lines` (~:775) — message emitted as one unwrapped `Line`.
- `render_detail` (~:327) — `Paragraph` without `Wrap`, blanket-applied to
  every line in the box, including the message line that does not need
  column alignment.

The no-wrap constraint is only real for the source-line + caret-row pair. The
message line is free text and should wrap.

## Fix (sketch)
- Detail box: wrap the message line(s) ourselves at render time — soft-wrap
  the message into N lines at inner width, indented to the message column, so
  the caret alignment of the other rows is untouched (do **not** turn on
  `Wrap` for the whole Paragraph). Feed the wrapped count into
  `detail_box_height` so the box grows (respecting the existing 8-row cap) and
  make the detail box scrollable when the message exceeds the cap.
- List rows: keep the ellipsis (rows must stay one/two lines), but guarantee a
  usable floor — the current `.max(4)` yields "abc…". Prefer shrinking the
  location field before the message, and in Relaxed mode allow the message to
  spill to a second row for the *selected* item.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Unit tests over the pure layout fns (no terminal needed) — this is how the
existing `fragment_rhs_no_truncate_when_room` tests work:

Red:
- `detail_message_wraps_at_narrow_width`: long message + narrow inner width →
  `pretty_detail_lines` returns >1 message line, none exceeding the width, and
  the concatenation equals the original message.
- `detail_box_height_grows_with_wrapped_message`: height accounts for the
  wrapped lines, capped at 8 inner rows.
- `caret_alignment_survives_wrapping`: the source line and caret row keep the
  same prefix width after the message wraps (regression guard for :327).

Variants (per CLAUDE.md: generalize the case):
- severities: error / warning / info / hint all wrap identically.
- densities: Compact and Relaxed list rows both ellipsize with a readable
  floor; assert `…` is present iff truncation happened.
- widths: sweep inner widths (e.g. 20, 40, 60, 100, 200) and assert no
  produced line exceeds the width and no message content is silently dropped
  without a `…` marker.
- long unbroken token (a 200-char identifier with no spaces) → hard-wraps
  instead of overflowing.
- multi-byte / wide chars in the message → wrap by display width, not by
  `chars().count()`, so no line overflows.
- empty and 1-char messages → no panic, no stray `…`.
- long `path:line:col` + short message in Compact → message still gets a
  usable budget (the location shrinks first).